course: dictionary
lesson: 11637
title: Words for everyday things
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An armrest is the part of a chair, sofa or seat where you rest your arm. You can find armrests on armchairs, in cinemas, and in cars, buses and planes. «Tom lifted the armrest so he could slide closer to the window.» Lifting it up tells you it can move, so it must be a part of the seat.
explain: Long words can be broken into smaller words. Armrest is made from two small words: arm and rest. Arm plus rest gives you the place where your arm rests. Always ask: does this word make sense when I think about its parts?
explain: Good manners matter on shared seats. «Sam let the lady next to him share the armrest on the long flight.» To share the armrest means both people rest their arms there kindly, without pushing into the other person's space.
fact: An armrest is the part of a seat where you rest your arm.
fact: Armrests are found on armchairs, sofas, cinema seats, and in cars, buses and planes.
fact: Armrest is a noun, and its plural is armrests.
fact: «Share the armrest» means let the person next to you rest their arm there too.
fact: Armrest is a compound word: arm + rest.
exercise: «Mum lifted the armrest so the baby could sit beside her.» What is an armrest? | The bag under the seat | The little table where you put your drink | The back of a chair | *The part of a seat where you rest your arm
exercise: «Please share the armrest with the lady next to you.» What does share the armrest mean? | Sit on the floor instead | *Let her rest her arm there too, kindly | Move the armrest off the bus | Take the whole seat for yourself
exercise: Armrest is a long word. Which two small words make it up? | car and rest | arm and back | *arm and rest | arm and seat
test: «Dad rested his arm on the armrest all the way home.» Where did Dad rest his arm? | In the boot | *On the seat part for his arm | On the floor | Under the window
test: Which seat is most likely to have an armrest? | *An armchair | A cloud | A pond | A football
exam: Ella says, «Can you lift the armrest, please?» What does Ella want you to do? | Sit down on the table | *Move up the part of the seat where you rest your arm | Put the bag on the floor | Open the car window
